\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 Search for the Rosetta Rock
\f1\b0\fs24 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 The Johnny had hardly lifted his head from his work since Sarah had laid down the law 2 months prior. He had resolved to hunker down and produce results before turning his mind to revenge. He would do as he was told and keep complaints to a minimum. He calculated a total absence of complaints would be noticed, so he would throw in a few here an there just to keep in character. He even managed to talk Dr Kathy into hiring a cryptologist, a mathematician, an Egyptologist, several varieties of physicists and and a few other boffins to his team of techs and accelerate the analysis. Although he was too self-absorbed to notice, the improved work ethic lead to actual efficiency, productivity and a degree of work place harmony. His underlings didn\'92t even want to kill him anymore. A decent maiming would more than suffice. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
Sarah and Dr Kathy had been a little distracted in recent weeks, with the poison-attack on the Elvi and related security concerns for Richard, they had not blessed him with their presence. With the imminent completion of the private residences Sarah, Richard and Dr Kathy were moving in at the end of the week. The remote location and high security of the facility made it a perfect site to ensure young Richard\'92s safety. Upon arrival, no doubt, they would expect a progress report that chronicled actual progress and he was confident his news would would not displease.
\f1 \

\f2 \
Eight weeks of hard slog by the entire team had confirmed the markings in the Beta-mode identifier pattern were indeed some sort of message. The oscillations in the blurred marking were not random but patterns repeated in parallel lines, many times over. Initially, it was hoped the message would be found in the manner of repetition, not unlike some heavenly Morse code, but those hopes were soon dashed. Simplistic thinking would not crack this code.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Could it be a musical scale?\'94 Asked Senior Technical Officer Vilnius Cambridge at the daily briefing. A hail of notebooks and palm devices bounced off his forehead. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93We\'92ve tried that.\'94 The Johnny said.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What about a logarithmic scale?\'94 Vilnius replied.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Give the music scales a break will you?\'94 For the moment Johnny kept his cool.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Well, we\'92ve got all the computer processing power in the world, making a billion calculations a second and for the last 2 months we have made virtually no progress.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I think it has something to do with gas chromatography.\'94 Said the physicist, Rosalind Frankland. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93No, light spectroscopy.\'94 Argued the resident astrophysicist.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Have either of you constructed a viable method of testing?\'94 The Johnny asked.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93No.\'94 They both replied. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93The Egyptian Hieroglyphs were thought meaningless until the discovery of the Rosetta Stone.\'94 Egyptologist\cf2  \cf0 added.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Thanks for the history lesson, but how does that help?\'94 The Johnny asked.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Perhaps we need a cypher key or code phrase.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Okay, I\'92ll order one today.\'94 The Johnny snapped back. \'93Problem solved.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93For the translation we wish to make, there is no telling what the equivalent of a Rosetta Stone is, but if it can be identified, the message will translate itself.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93So what you are saying is, we are searching for that elusive clue that will unlock the mystery?\'94 The Johnny managed to remain calm.\uc0\u8232 
\f1 \

\f2 \'93Yes.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93So how does that differ from what we are already doing?\'94 The Johnny screamed at the history buff. \'93We are going to solve this with hard work, trial and error, plenty of error and some luck. Let\'92s get to it.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
The next morning the senior management team met as usual for the morning briefing. Vilnius Cambridge\cf3  \cf0 was nursing a few cuts and bruises, courtesy of yesterday\'92s briefing and had resolved to remain silent. Particle Physicist, Dr Bradley Quark, was fidgeting and could not wait for The Johnny to open the meeting. \'93I have been working on imaging. At ultra microscopic level the message have thousands of parallel markings with blurred, but delineated micro-grooves, sort of like a recording on those old black dics.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Like they used to record music on\'94 Vilnius felt vindicated until the first notepad struck the bridge of his nose. He managed to duck the rest.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93You see people, our physicist has made an interesting observation. It may amount to nothing, but it is worth following up.\'94 Johnny winced. He was not used to praising anyone, apart from himself. \'93Much better than Rosetta stone platitudes.\'94\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I\'92ve got more news.\'94 The physicist said. \'93The images are blurred because they are slightly out of phase. If as you claim this is message is from before the big bang, I thought it may be from another universe, a universe where the universal gravitational constant is different.\'94\cf3  
\f1 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'93There are 26 fundamental constants that describe the universe, how did you decide upon the gravitational constant?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93The discs are said to operate on gravity waves, I just figured it was a good starting point. I just got lucky.\'94 The physicist admitted. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93How lucky?\'94 The Johnny was actually interested.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I have only had time to do a quick analysis of two messages, but there are some interesting findings.\'94 He switch on the holo-screen and pointed to an equation floating in the space before them. \'93As you know the universal gravitational constant is expressed by \'85\'85.
\f1 \
{\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename Clipboard Image}\picw586\pich80\picwgoal8790\pichgoal1200\pngblip }}\

\f2 \
\
\'85\'85I filtered the images through a phase variance compensator and I have calculated, from the degree of variance, this message is from a universe with a slightly higher universal gravitational constant. When I tried to replicate the process with another message, I found the phase variance was different again, with the Universal Gravitational constant slightly lower than our universe.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Good work, doctor.\'94 The Johnny tried to be cool but he was reeling. 
\f3\i Different universes!
\f2\i0  \'93Congratulations, Dr Quark. We can actually report some real progress. How long until you can examine all of the messages?
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Well, if we share the load equally, we should only have 500 or 600 each to examine. If we can get more two more phase variance compensators, we should be finished before the end of the month.\'94 Dr Quark replied.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Excellent.\'94 The Johnny stood and leaned across the table, offering his hand to Dr Quark. The Doctor took it hesitantly, but firmly and glanced at his colleagues, each of whom wore jaws agape. \'93You have made my day.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Thank you, Johnny\'94 Dr Quark replied. The Johnny halted the handshake, mid-pump. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What of the other 25 universal constants? The fine structure constant? The strong coupling constant? Neutrino mixing Parameters? Quark Mixing parameters?\'94 The Johnny stopped at that one. He saw a few of the lab coats chuckle. 
\f3\i You don\'92t get to call me Johnny. 
\f1\i0 \

\f2 \
\'93I am well aware of the quark mixing parameters.\'94 Dr Quark sighed. He had had his fill of quark jokes. \'93I have not been able to cast my mind to the other constants, but my impression is they are probably not too different. Also, I would think if gravity is different in the other universes, time may also pass at a different rate.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93When you have checked all of the messages, start on the other universal constants and get back to me.\'94 The Johnny left the room without another word.
\f1 \

\f2 \
 
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0  - - -
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
The Elvis Security Teams descended on the facility 2 weeks prior to Sarah\'92s expected arrival and augmented the high security facility with state of the art automated defence systems, courtesy of Eloise Shakti. The entire complex was swept for bombs, booby-traps, weapons, listening devices, secret cameras and tin cans with lengths of string between them. Satisfied all was secure the interior designers were summoned, Elvi all, and took to the task of turning the sterile canvas into a warm, inviting home. Desperate to satisfy the needs of the fast growing Richard, each decision was debated, argued, altered, changed back and the cause of much pain. Surprisingly, the result was a beautiful and tasteful interior with light pastels contrasting the furnishing and ornate trim work. To everyone\'92s surprise it filtered through that Alexander Shakti was to join Sarah and Richard at the facility. According to the scuttlebutt he had arranged for time away from the office to finalise his report on Director ??? Murder. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
Sarah and Richard, especially Richard, were ecstatic with their new home. Sarah had resigned herself to something similar to upmarket camping, but the residence was spacious and included with every domestic device imaginable - devices to make easy tasks easier, but with proportionally crappier results. There was, however, no time for home making and Sarah arranged a meeting with The Johnny and Dr Kathy to get the first update she had received in a couple of weeks. She left Shakti to his complaints about how hard reports were to write and headed for her meeting. She had seen how hard he had been working, reading and re-reading transcripts, examining financial statements, computer activity and communication logs. She had offered assistance that he no doubt needed, but he had been determined to solve this one on his own, but was yet to identify a suspect.
\f1 \

\f2 \
Sarah walked briskly and confidently into the conference room, Richard bouncing off her hip and holding on tight. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Does he have to be here?\'94 The Johnny asked. \'93Don\'92t let him touch anything.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Richard never leaves my side.\'94 Sarah reminded him as she place her boy on the floor. Richard scooted across the floor to the nearest Elvi and begged to be picked up. The lucky Elvis gladly obliged.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I was talking about Shakti.\'94 Laughter filler the room. Even Sarah and Richard had a good chuckle at that one. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93You are in a good mood, aren\'92t you?\'94 Sarah joined Dr Kathy and The Johnny at the table.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What about the Brylcreem security team?\'94 The Johnny asked. \'93Do they have to stay?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93You try to get them to leave.\'94 Sarah challenged. \'93What do you think Team Leader?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Anyone interfering with our sacred task of protecting the great one will be neutralised.\'94 Team Leader Elvis replied without hesitation. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93\'94Let\'92s get started shall we?\'94 Dr Kathy Logan was keen to get this over and done with and get on to the serious task of getting fucked up. \'93Johnny? Can you give us an update?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I have some marvelous news.\'94 The Johnny smiled broadly and ran his finger across the pink cicatrice on his skull. \'93We have confirmed that the pattern is comprised of messages, multiple separate message from multiple alternate universes.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf3 The room was silent for an eternity until Richard started laughing loudly and clapping his hands madly. Sarah joined in, as did Kathy and the Security Team. Sarah felt a pure happiness beaming from Richard\'92s little chest and could not help but join in. It was clear Richard understood the implications of what had been said and he too thought it was marvelous.
\f1 \cf0 \

\f2 \cf3 \
\'93If you want to check the figures, I think you will confirm my results.\'94 The Johnny wasn\'92t expecting laughter. 
\f1 \cf0 \

\f2 \cf3 \
Sarah laughed, not in disbelief, but in the sheer joy of a scientific discovery of this magnitude and of course the fact that everyone else laughed, making it even funnier. Confirming the multi-verse theory, or perhaps the big bang-big crunch theory, was a significant leap forward. 
\f1 \cf0 \

\f2 \cf3 \
\'93I believe you!\'94 Sarah sputtered out
\f1 \cf0 \

\f2 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \'93When you examine the details in the report you will see that Dr Quark identified the messages each originated from places with different values for the Universal Gravitational Constant. Multiple alternate universes!\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What of the messages themselves?\'94 Dr Kathy asked, finally able to speak after the gob-smacking and for some reason funny news she had just heard. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93We are no closer to translating, but Dr Quark discovered, just this morning, fundamental particles also have a slightly different electron volt values, except for the Higgs Boson. We don\'92t know, yet, if it will assist us in any practical way.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
The remainder of the meeting was spent on menial, but vital, arrangements relating to rostering, office supplies, overtime (there would be none) personal protective equipment, radiation shielding for food supplies. Shakti was to remain in the residential wing, unless accompanied by an adult. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
Richard took his first steps inside the residence and unlike his father, soon had the run of the entire complex. Sarah quickly gave up chasing him and left it to the security teams and nannies to keep him under control. He had the knack of teetering in on important meetings and most particularly, when The Johnny was conducting an experiments in the laboratory wing. Richard was always under foot, but never in the way and The Johnny, much to his chagrin, had to privately admit the child was very bright. Yet to say a word, Richard would smile when he heard something he liked, would frown for anything to his disliked and would cry if he disagreed or needed his nappy changed. He soon had the scientists well trained and taking instructions, his delightful disposition unable to be resisted. The team had to admit the little upstart had been right on every occasion he had intervened with a tantrum, which would not stop until a decision or nappy was changed. Sometimes both.
\f1 \

\f2 \
Security teams were perpetually on alert keeping up with the little dynamo, but none could think of anything more worthwhile to do with their lives than keeping him safe. There was nothing random in the nature of Richard\'92s wanderings and once he had sufficient gross motor function he began to run everywhere. Firstly he fell and tripped and screamed in frustration, too impatient to await fine motor  function in his feet and toes to catch up, but after many falls he finally began to run. He ran and ran, but not for the sake of running. Any objective observer would conclude he was training and when his upper body strength started to kick in, he confirmed this by commencing a regimen of push ups and arm curls. It did not go unnoticed that he was developing fast, very fast and grew noticeably larger by the day. It was calculated by one of the more inquisitive minds in the team that Richard was growing at 5 times the rate of an average child. This came as no surprise, Richard was anything but average. Initially there was some degree of concern that Richard\'92s cognition could not keep pace with the physical development, but his astonishing mind easily maintained the pace.
\f1 \

\f2 \
He was sneaky as he was smart and quickly learned to ditch his security teams and was forever being located in obscure nooks and crannies, somehow managing to defeat the security grid. On more than one occasion he has found in the test bunker examining the markings burnt into the concrete ceiling and walls of the vast empty space. Against the advice of the Elvi Security themselves, Sarah rejected calls to have him locked down with his dad. Apart from the cruel nature of such close proximity with Shakti, she thought there must be a reason for his infant-reconnoiters and suggested the Elvi should get on with doing their job. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0 - - - 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The Elvi War Cabinet had again been called together for an emergency session to debate possible action in response to the genocide attempt by the PTD. Anger of the entire Elvi nation was focused the CEO and the Directorate of Proactive Euthanasia and Pre-emptive Reciprocity. The Elvi were ready to heat up this cold war.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93We have been very lucky.\'94 Said the Minister of Health. \'93Not one death. We must be very grateful to the Blessed Mother and the protection of the Hybrid T-Virus. Many are still gravely ill, but seem to be recovering.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93The lack of deaths does not reduce their culpability!\'94 Reminded the Justice Minister. \'93Their intent was clear. Annihilation of us all.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93We have already struck back at the PTD.\'94 The High Elvis announced, \'93The Blessed Mother, some little time ago attacked them on our behalf and has caused significant damage. Financial losses are now only rippling through the economy. She has reduced the total wealth of the PTD by 20% and increased our holdings by 500%. Many of our most ardent enemies have been financially ruined. We have reports that the CEO himself is close to bankruptcy and desperate for funds.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93They must pay with their lives.\'94 The Minister of War called out from across the table. \'93We have negotiated contracts to purchase arms from our saviour\'92s grandmother. All next generation firepower. They will have nothing the match us.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Until she sells the PTD the same weaponry.\'94 Cracker, the Great Teacher, pointed out. \'93She may be an ally, but a sale is a sale. There are few things more important to the powerful than the bottom line.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93We have plans in place, we have the weapons and we have the will.\'94 The Minister of war barked back.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93And what do we do after we win?\'94 The High Elvis posed. \'93I don\'92t want to preside over the PTD. Do you? That is a nightmare I wish to avoid. I am only interested in promoting our interests and our culture. It is far better to hit them where is hurts - in the pocket book.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93What of the CEO?\'94 The Minister for War wanted some blood to be spilt. He deserves more than mere poverty.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93The CEO must answer to the Board of Directors. With the recent spate of bankruptcies the membership of the board has changed considerably and I am assured the majority are sympathetic to our cause.  Indeed, some of them are out largest investors. An insolvent CEO will never be allowed to continue.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93You are mistaken, High Elvis. For the ultra-wealthy, bankruptcy is a momentary inconvenience.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley joined in. She knew how slippery her people could be. \'93We will need much more than a lack of liquidity to bring him down. Someone will make a deal, prop him up financially and have themselves a puppet. No, we will need to be something the elites will not forgive.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Do we know who his replacement might be?\'94 The Minister of War was not convinced. \'93Better the devil you know.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93It is my fondest hope it will be Eloise Shakti.\'94 The High Elvis said proudly. \'93She may not be Elvis, but she will do anything to protect our saviour. I expect she will act in self interest, until in conflicts with her vow to protect Richard.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I agree, up to a certain point. I am willing to bet she has her price.\'94 The Great Teacher suggested. \'93I propose no action be taken until the next meeting of the Board of Directors. There is no need for war.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I agree.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley said. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93We vote.\'94 The High Elvis said.
\f1 \

\f2 \
The vote was close, but The Great Teacher and the Holy Aunt managed to keep the peace in the PTD, at least in the short term. The meeting was adjourned and they all went out for cocktails and a show. After siphoning alcohol at an alarming rate over several hours, a drunken Great Teacher staggered away from the Quarter and slowly traversed half the city to his palace inside Hardy Tower 1. He did not notice the two well dressed goons following.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0 - - -
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \
\
The Jacobson-Shakti clan had settled into a routine and quickly began to resemble an average, level 5, dysfunctional family. Both parents worked hard or at least one of them worked hard and Shakti wasted a ton of time staring at files not understanding a thing. The level 5 progeny, in the traditional fashion, was largely left to his own devices and spent his time training and studying every educational data base he could stream. He was not permitted to get his hands on a brain-dump set, one task the Elvi had not failed in, and had embraced reading books, both electronic and hardbacks. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
He firstly taught himself to read and then took on simple high school level material, but soon was devouring university texts. In a few weeks, while dad struggled to add two and two, the mute genius amassed the equivalent knowledge of doctorates in Quantum Physics, Mathematics and Biology.
\f1 \

\f2 \
Similarly, a routine had broken out throughout the complex. There was an air of optimism within the research team and each knew if they stuck to their tasks and crunch the numbers, they would succeed. Fame and fortune would surely follow. With the unexpected outbreak of harmony, Sarah found she had a some time on her hands and decided to interrupt Richard\'92s self-education and get in some quality time. She thought he would enjoy the simple pleasure of playing with brightly coloured toys and stuffed bears, but Richard had no interest in things puerile and simply wandered off, leaving mum to her toys.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93That went well.\'94 Sarah sighed as she got up off the floor. She had figured she would become an embarrassment to her son when he was 14, not 14 months. She then caught a glimpse of Shakti\'92s open files hovering above his desk as the holo-emitter softly hummed. Shakti had worked all night again and would be asleep for many hours. She sat down and began to read, jumping artfully from data base to data base and by cross matching the finance and communication records, she was soon shaking her head in disbelief. The suspect was clear and she only needed to reconstruct a deleted video file and she would have the case wrapped up. Reconstructing dead files was something of which she had gained considerable experience when tracking down Emile Kalheri and she soon turned white noise into high definition holo-vid. She had to admit, Shakti had done a great job of collecting the evidence, all of the information was there, someone just had to take a look. A proper look.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Alexander?\'94 Sarah asked Shakti over afternoon tea. \'93With all of that information you have, do you have any suspects?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Yes, but I don\'92t want to say. You will think it is stupid.\'94 Shakti said, hoping she would not press for an answer.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Tell me, please.\'94 Sarah said, taking a dainty sip of tea.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Alright. Promise you won\'92t laugh.\'94 He waited until she nodded. \'93The CEO.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
Sarah spat her tea back into her cup, coughing and spluttering. 
\f3\i He actually worked it out!
\f1\i0 \

\f2 \
 \'93I asked you not to laugh.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93I\'92m not laughing. I believe you, trust me.\'94 She then made a call the the Commissioner\'92s office. 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0 - - -
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \
\'93Good Morning Commissioner.\'94 A cheerful Sarah said on being connected.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Hi, Sarah. How can I help you today?\'94 Commissioner Hayley Lanning, the Holy Aunt, was pleased to hear from Sarah. There had been nothing but good news since she finally took over the lab facilities and Hayley was happy to plough more resources into the operation. \'93Any problems with Johnny?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93No, everything seems to running smoothly here and they are making progress every day. I am actually calling about Alex.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Who?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Shakti.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Yes, of course. Has he finished that report yet? It\'92s months overdue.\'94 Hayley dropped into Commissioner mode.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93He thinks the CEO was behind it and I think he\'92s right.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Don\'92t be absurd.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93No, but I had a good look at the date and did a little digging and was able to raise a deleted communications file and security files.\'94 Sarah paused for a moment. \'93It is the entire call between the CEO and Director ??? It records the murder and it is clear the CEO directing the events. I am sending you the file now.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
Instantaneously a hologram of the CEO and Director ??? formed above Hayley\'92s desk. The hologram of the CEO was hovering above the CEO\'92s desk when the Office Manager burst in and fired one clean shot to the forehead of the Director, killing him instantly. Within a few moments, the Office Manager had placed the gun barrel to her temple and fired without hesitation. \'93Excellent\'94 the floating head commented and then disappeared only to return a few minutes later claiming he knew not what had happened. There was no doubt the CEO was behind the murder of Director XXXX and the death of the office manager.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Well, it looks like we have our man and this is very timely indeed.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93No.\'94 Sarah said. \'93Lieutenant Alexander Shakti has his man.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Sarah, he can\'92t be involved in this, now. It\'92s too important.\'94 
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Just let him do the arrest. You will be there to hold his hand, but let him take the credit.\'94 Sarah earnestly felt Shakti deserve a break. \'93Don\'92t let him speak to the press, he\'92s hopeless without a cue-cards.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Okay, he gets to say \'91you\'92re under arrest\'92 and that is it.\'94 Hayley countered. \'93Does he know he\'92s cracked the case yet?\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93No, I will go through it with him now.\'94 Sarah knew explaining it to him would take some significant time. \'93I\'92ll send him over tomorrow morning and you can make your plans.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Okay. I expect to see Shakti in my office at 7.00am tomorrow.\'94 Hayley said. \'93I think we will drop in on the Board of Directors meeting.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93Maximise his embarrassment?\'94 Sarah asked.
\f1 \

\f2 \
\'93You got it.\'94
\f1 \

\f2 \
